<https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/claim/morphoeval-streichan-global-morphogenetic-flow> a pk:Claim ;
    rdfs:label "Streichan et al. (2018), Mayer et al. (2010) & Lefebvre et al. (2023) Drosophila global morphogenetic flow & active nematic myosin tensor mechanics (Drosophila melanogaster (whole-embryo cellular blastoderm & germband extension stages 6-8))",
        "Streichan et al. (2018), Mayer et al. (2010) & Lefebvre et al. (2023) Drosophila global morphogenetic flow & active nematic myosin tensor mechanics faithfully reproduces Drosophila melanogaster (whole-embryo cellular blastoderm & germband extension stages 6-8) morphology" ;
    dct:conformsTo <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/math-law/streichan-global-morphogenetic-flow-1>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/math-law/streichan-global-morphogenetic-flow-2>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/math-law/streichan-global-morphogenetic-flow-3> ;
    dct:description "The simulation script(s) 2018-streichan-global-morphogenetic-flow.py implement the cited source model as published and produce forms that match real Drosophila melanogaster (whole-embryo cellular blastoderm & germband extension stages 6-8) specimens and the source authors' figures. A belief under audit, not a fact: its credibility is the weight of evidence (MorphoEval 0.1.0 overall 92.3/100, audit 2026-10-19-global-morphogenetic-flow-audit-v2) and the assessments." ;
    dct:subject <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/317bc3c/2018-streichan-global-morphogenetic-flow.py> ;
    schema:about "Drosophila melanogaster (whole-embryo cellular blastoderm & germband extension stages 6-8)" ;
    schema:additionalProperty "does_not_claim: Discrete vertex-level T1 rosette topology transitions or 3D yolk-sac internal Stokes fluid-structure coupling",
        "reconstructed_in_script: 64x48 2D spectral Helmholtz longitudinal-transverse compressible Stokes-Brinkman PDE solver on the 500x420 um cartographic Drosophila blastoderm domain (Green's function L2 relative error = 1.62e-16), 30 min Lagrangian germband marker advection, 6-regime wild-type and mutant benchmark, and 15x15 (ell_H x eta_b/eta) parameter morphospace",
        "reconstructed_in_script: Automated computer-vision contour, pair-rule stripe, DV cable gradient anisotropy, and posterior midgut invagination fold segmentation on drosophila_germband_extension_specimen.jpg (IDR0151, AP/DV = 2.3853 vs 2.3810 biological, 8 stripes, spacing = 75.86 px, solidity = 0.9383)",
        "reported_in_source: Mayer et al. (2010) Nature 467:617-621 hydrodynamic screening length ell_H = sqrt(eta/xi) and Lefebvre et al. (2023) eLife 12:e78787 geometric control of Myosin-II nematic orientation and maternal bcd nos tsl / pair-rule eve mutant flow collapse",
        "reported_in_source: Streichan, Lefebvre, Noppe, Hufnagel & Shraiman (2018) eLife 7:e27454 compressible viscous Stokes-Brinkman PDE eta*nabla^2 v + eta_b*nabla(nabla.v) - (eta/ell_H^2)*v = -nabla.sigma^a demonstrating that DV-polarized junctional Myosin-II cables plus isotropic posterior midgut invagination predict >90% (r = 0.924) of global embryonic tissue velocity",
        "transfer_boundary: 2D cartographic cylindrical/ellipsoidal spectral Stokes-Brinkman continuum sheet calibrated to Streichan et al. (2018) SPIM light-sheet PIV velocity fields and Clark et al. (2022) IDR0151 confocal blastoderm geometry" ;
    pk:aristotelianEfficientCause "5. Vertex / Potts / Nematics" ;
    pk:aristotelianMegistonGenos "II. Anaima (Invertebrata)" ;
    pk:aristotelianPoionForm "Polygonal Packing & Furrows" ;
    pk:aristotelianPosonLaw "Shape Index p_0* = 3.813" ;
    pk:aristotelianSubalternClass "Entoma (Arthropoda)" ;
    pk:biologicalGenus "Drosophila" ;
    pk:context "script(s): https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/317bc3c/2018-streichan-global-morphogenetic-flow.py; output: docs/media/global_morphogenetic_flow_comparison.png; organism: Drosophila melanogaster (whole-embryo cellular blastoderm & germband extension stages 6-8); checkpoint commit: https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/commit/317bc3c; environment: python 3.14.7, numpy 2.4.2, scipy 1.17.0, matplotlib 3.10.8, Pillow 12.1.1; spec_fingerprint: c6f91e927b85c9e6c96461d53e4ae9c082d9c0ad9d74ed650b6b2f21fb08b782; artifact_sha256: c2b12d9cc11f49cbc76202021e27a120ea25ff2713abd4ee312c77cb90e82127; input_dataset_sha256: {datasets/global_morphogenetic_flow/drosophila_germband_extension_specimen.jpg=2d7fad8f57edcadf..., datasets/global_morphogenetic_flow/global_morphogenetic_flow_reference.json=160ead86ff9c447b..., datasets/global_morphogenetic_flow/scout_manifest.json=990f3ea83019f3d1...}; supersedes_audit_id: 2026-10-19-global-morphogenetic-flow-audit; claim_boundary: [reported_in_source: Streichan, Lefebvre, Noppe, Hufnagel & Shraiman (2018) eLife 7:e27454 compressible viscous Stokes-Brinkman PDE eta*nabla^2 v + eta_b*nabla(nabla.v) - (eta/ell_H^2)*v = -nabla.sigma^a demonstrating that DV-polarized junctional Myosin-II cables plus isotropic posterior midgut invagination predict >90% (r = 0.924) of global embryonic tissue velocity | Mayer et al. (2010) Nature 467:617-621 hydrodynamic screening length ell_H = sqrt(eta/xi) and Lefebvre et al. (2023) eLife 12:e78787 geometric control of Myosin-II nematic orientation and maternal bcd nos tsl / pair-rule eve mutant flow collapse; reconstructed_in_script: 64x48 2D spectral Helmholtz longitudinal-transverse compressible Stokes-Brinkman PDE solver on the 500x420 um cartographic Drosophila blastoderm domain (Green's function L2 relative error = 1.62e-16), 30 min Lagrangian germband marker advection, 6-regime wild-type and mutant benchmark, and 15x15 (ell_H x eta_b/eta) parameter morphospace | Automated computer-vision contour, pair-rule stripe, DV cable gradient anisotropy, and posterior midgut invagination fold segmentation on drosophila_germband_extension_specimen.jpg (IDR0151, AP/DV = 2.3853 vs 2.3810 biological, 8 stripes, spacing = 75.86 px, solidity = 0.9383); transfer_boundary: 2D cartographic cylindrical/ellipsoidal spectral Stokes-Brinkman continuum sheet calibrated to Streichan et al. (2018) SPIM light-sheet PIV velocity fields and Clark et al. (2022) IDR0151 confocal blastoderm geometry; does_not_claim: Discrete vertex-level T1 rosette topology transitions or 3D yolk-sac internal Stokes fluid-structure coupling]" ;
    pk:derivedFromPaper <https://doi.org/10.1038/nature09376>,
        <https://doi.org/10.7554/eLife.27454>,
