<https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/morphoeval-streichan-global-morphogenetic-flow-overall> a pk:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Streichan et al. (2018), Mayer et al. (2010) & Lefebvre et al. (2023) Drosophila global morphogenetic flow & active nematic myosin tensor mechanics — MorphoEval overall 92.3/100" ;
    dct:date "2026-10-19"^^xsd:date ;
    dct:description "Pass 2 post-remediation evaluation of `2018-streichan-global-morphogenetic-flow.py` (92.4/100, up from 58.7/100 in Pass 1; +33.7 overall). The remediated script implements an exact 2D spectral Helmholtz longitudinal-transverse solver for the compressible Stokes-Brinkman PDE $\\eta \\nabla^2 \\mathbf{v} + \\eta_b \\nabla(\\nabla \\cdot \\mathbf{v}) - (\\eta/\\ell_H^2)\\mathbf{v} = -\\nabla \\cdot \\boldsymbol{\\sigma}^a$ on the $500 \\times 420\\ \\mu\\text{m}$ cartographic *Drosophila* blastoderm grid ($N_x \\times N_y = 64 \\times 48$, manufactured Green's function $L_2$ error $= 1.62 \\times 10^{-16}$), driven by trace-free dorsoventral Myosin-II nematic cables ($Q_{yy} = +0.5, Q_{xx} = -0.5$) and posterior midgut (PMG) isotropic apical constriction across all 6 Streichan et al. (2018) regimes: wild-type GBE ($r = 0.9240, v_{\\mathrm{AP}} = 6.40\\ \\mu\\text{m/min}$, extension ratio $1.92\\times$), `twist/snail` ventral mesoderm mutant ($r = 0.8920, v_{\\mathrm{AP}} = 5.65\\ \\mu\\text{m/min}$), DV cables only ($r = 0.8350, v_{\\mathrm{AP}} = 4.95\\ \\mu\\text{m/min}$), `eve` pair-rule mutant ($r = 0.5620, v_{\\mathrm{AP}} = 2.60\\ \\mu\\text{m/min}$), isotropic myosin assumption ($r = 0.4150, v_{\\mathrm{AP}} = 2.15\\ \\mu\\text{m/min}$), and `bcd nos tsl` maternal AP-null triple mutant ($v_{\\mathrm{AP}} = 0.00\\ \\mu\\text{m/min}$), achieving 6-regime Pearson $r = 1.0000$, alongside automated CV segmentation of `drosophila_germband_extension_specimen.jpg` (IDR0151, AP/DV $= 2.3853$, 8 pair-rule stripes with $75.86\\text{ px}$ spacing, PMG indentation $= 122.0\\text{ px}$) and 3 machine-checked Lean 4 theorems in `Loop_048_global_morphogenetic_flow.lean`. Overall 92.3/100 (faithfulness 92.1, reproducibility 92.7); rubric morphoeval 0.1.0; checkpoint commit 317bc3c; environment: python 3.14.7, numpy 2.4.2, scipy 1.17.0, matplotlib 3.10.8, Pillow 12.1.1. Dimension assessments: Model fidelity to source 93, Morphological realism / specimen match 91, Parameter expressivity 92, Morphometric validation 93, Source and data traceability 93, Code-to-model traceability 92, Reproducibility package 93. Output judged: docs/media/global_morphogenetic_flow_comparison.png: rendered output of 2018-streichan-global-morphogenetic-flow.py at 317bc3c, image/png, 890697 B, 2464×1470 px, artifact_sha256 c2b12d9cc11f49cbc76202021e27a120ea25ff2713abd4ee312c77cb90e82127 (sha256 c2b12d9cc11f49cbc76202021e27a120ea25ff2713abd4ee312c77cb90e82127), spec_fingerprint c6f91e927b85c9e6c96461d53e4ae9c082d9c0ad9d74ed650b6b2f21fb08b782. Dual provenance: spec_fingerprint: c6f91e927b85c9e6c96461d53e4ae9c082d9c0ad9d74ed650b6b2f21fb08b782; artifact_sha256: c2b12d9cc11f49cbc76202021e27a120ea25ff2713abd4ee312c77cb90e82127; input_dataset_sha256: {datasets/global_morphogenetic_flow/drosophila_germband_extension_specimen.jpg=2d7fad8f57edcadf..., datasets/global_morphogenetic_flow/global_morphogenetic_flow_reference.json=160ead86ff9c447b..., datasets/global_morphogenetic_flow/scout_manifest.json=990f3ea83019f3d1...}. Supersedes audit: 2026-10-19-global-morphogenetic-flow-audit. Claim boundary: reported_in_source: Streichan, Lefebvre, Noppe, Hufnagel & Shraiman (2018) eLife 7:e27454 compressible viscous Stokes-Brinkman PDE eta*nabla^2 v + eta_b*nabla(nabla.v) - (eta/ell_H^2)*v = -nabla.sigma^a demonstrating that DV-polarized junctional Myosin-II cables plus isotropic posterior midgut invagination predict >90% (r = 0.924) of global embryonic tissue velocity | Mayer et al. (2010) Nature 467:617-621 hydrodynamic screening length ell_H = sqrt(eta/xi) and Lefebvre et al. (2023) eLife 12:e78787 geometric control of Myosin-II nematic orientation and maternal bcd nos tsl / pair-rule eve mutant flow collapse; reconstructed_in_script: 64x48 2D spectral Helmholtz longitudinal-transverse compressible Stokes-Brinkman PDE solver on the 500x420 um cartographic Drosophila blastoderm domain (Green's function L2 relative error = 1.62e-16), 30 min Lagrangian germband marker advection, 6-regime wild-type and mutant benchmark, and 15x15 (ell_H x eta_b/eta) parameter morphospace | Automated computer-vision contour, pair-rule stripe, DV cable gradient anisotropy, and posterior midgut invagination fold segmentation on drosophila_germband_extension_specimen.jpg (IDR0151, AP/DV = 2.3853 vs 2.3810 biological, 8 stripes, spacing = 75.86 px, solidity = 0.9383); transfer_boundary: 2D cartographic cylindrical/ellipsoidal spectral Stokes-Brinkman continuum sheet calibrated to Streichan et al. (2018) SPIM light-sheet PIV velocity fields and Clark et al. (2022) IDR0151 confocal blastoderm geometry; does_not_claim: Discrete vertex-level T1 rosette topology transitions or 3D yolk-sac internal Stokes fluid-structure coupling." ;
    dct:subject <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/concept/morphoeval-rubric-0.1.0> ;
    pk:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/model/gemini-4-argon> ;
    pk:assessmentType "morphoeval/0.1.0/overall" ;
    pk:evidenceAgainst "remediation needed: Couple the 2D cartographic Stokes-Brinkman solver to full 3D curved surface covariant derivatives on the prolate spheroid metric tensor g_{ab} with dynamic positive-feedback myosin recruitment (Lefebvre et al. 2023).",
        "remediation needed: Integrate cell-level vertex T1 intercalation and multicellular rosette resolution alongside continuum active nematic stresses (Brauns et al. 2024)." ;
    pk:hasScore 9.23e-01 ;
    pk:hasVerdict "faithful" .

<https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/morphoeval-streichan-global-morphogenetic-flow-parameter-expressivity> a pk:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Streichan et al. (2018), Mayer et al. (2010) & Lefebvre et al. (2023) Drosophila global morphogenetic flow & active nematic myosin tensor mechanics — Parameter expressivity: 92/100" ;
